      "mentions": 24,
      "title": {
        "en": "Emergency staff with polarized evaluations"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Many pet owners praise attending veterinarians and night technicians for urgent interventions that saved their pets' lives during traumatic crises. Grateful clients describe specific doctors as compassionate and thorough when dealing with acute pain. However, numerous reviews criticise front-desk personnel for callous attitudes, lack of empathy during bereavement, and combative administrative encounters."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "prices",
      "sentiment": "negative",
      "mentions": 12,
      "title": {
        "en": "Widespread dissatisfaction with emergency billing"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Clients frequently complain about aggressive billing practices, citing high walk-in examination fees and escalating invoices reaching several thousand dollars. Several reviewers felt pressured into redundant diagnostics and medications or reported disputed charges when requested updates were not supplied. While some acknowledge emergency veterinary medicine is naturally costly, most describe fees as excessive."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "communication",
      "sentiment": "negative",
      "mentions": 12,
      "title": {
        "en": "Repeated gaps in client communication"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet owners consistently report difficulty obtaining timely medical updates while companion animals undergo emergency observation. Multiple reviewers describe unreturned phone messages, unmonitored text messaging channels, and delayed diagnostic records needed by referral hospitals. Distressed clients express deep frustration over abrupt telephone interactions during critical family emergencies."
      }
    }
  ],
